<title>SOUTH AFRICA: SAfrican Board issues 7,700 T maize export permits.</title>
<headline>SAfrican Board issues 7,700 T maize export permits.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1996-10-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Africa's Maize Board said on Wednesday it had issued permits to private traders for the export of 7,700 tonnes of maize in the period November 1 until December 31, 1996.  </p>
<p>It said the permits covered 3,900 tonnes of white maize and 3,800 tonnes of yellow maize.  </p>
<p>South African private maize traders have this season (May-April) in total received permits to export 1.473 million tonnes of white and yellow maize, the Maize Board said.</p>
<p>According to this season's maize scheme, traders may export up to 1.8 million tonnes of maize.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom 27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
